From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sechost: Deliver hosted drivers' device events in the
 process.

A process that runs its own drivers (wine_ntoskrnl_host_start, patch
0952) has no plug and play service. ntoskrnl's device events went to that
service over RPC and were lost, and sechost's notification thread gave up
when it could not reach it. A device that came or went while a program ran
was never announced to the windows and callbacks that asked for device
notifications: DBT_DEVICEARRIVAL and DBT_DEVICEREMOVECOMPLETE never came.
Programs that look for a new controller only when told (SDL's joystick
code, Windows.Gaming.Input, many engines) never found one connected after
they started.

Before its drivers start, a hosting ntoskrnl now finds sechost's new
__wine_queue_device_event, calls it once to say that device events come
from this process, and from then on hands it each event in place of the
RPC. sechost queues the event for the registrations made so far, and its
notification thread delivers the queue through the same filters and
callbacks as the service's events. The driver's thread only queues: a
window callback runs on the notification thread, so a program that opens
the new device from its handler does not wait on the driver loop that is
sending the event. Anywhere else nothing changes.
---
 dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/ntoskrnl.c         |  14 ++++
 dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/ntoskrnl_private.h |   2 +
 dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/pnp.c              |   7 ++
 dlls/sechost/sechost.spec            |   1 +
 dlls/sechost/service.c               | 143 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 5 files changed, 149 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

